</style></head><body class="sr-page"><div class="rd-app rd-study"><a class="rd-skip" href="#research-main">Skip to content</a><aside class="rd-sidebar"><a class="rd-brand" href="../index.html" aria-label="Capstone research dashboards"><span class="rd-brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">C</span><span>CAPSTONE<small>RESEARCH INTELLIGENCE</small></span></a><nav class="rd-navigation" aria-label="Research dashboards"><div class="rd-nav-group"><p>Sentiment monitor</p><a href="index.html"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Research overview</a><a href="crowding-tracker.html"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Market radar</a><a href="cnn-next-week.html"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Fear &amp; Greed</a><a href="daily-brief.html"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Daily briefing</a></div><div class="rd-nav-group"><p>Stocks &amp; evidence</p><a href="score-returns.html"><span aria-hidden="true">05</span>Score &amp; returns</a><a href="specialist-sales.html"><span aria-hidden="true">06</span>Specialist sales</a><a href="narrative-diffusion.html"><span aria-hidden="true">07</span>Narrative research</a></div><div class="rd-nav-group"><p>Methodology</p><a href="cnn-spy-qqq-study.html"><span aria-hidden="true">08</span>CNN · full study</a></div></nav><div class="rd-sidebar-footer">MARKET RESEARCH<small>CNN · Bloomberg · X · specialist sales</small><a href="../openrouter.html#token-growth">AI demand monitor <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="../index.html">All research dashboards <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></aside><div class="rd-workspace"><header class="rd-topbar"><div><p>RESEARCH / MARKET SENTIMENT</p><h1>Score study · research update</h1></div><div class="rd-actions"><span class="rd-asof">Price snapshot<b>2026-09-28</b></span><button type="button" class="rd-theme" aria-label="Switch to dark theme" aria-pressed="false"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.5 13A8.5 8.5 0 0 1 11 3.5 8.5 8.5 0 1 0 20.5 13Z"/></svg></button></div></header><main id="research-main" tabindex="-1"><h1>Score and subsequent returns</h1><p style="white-space:pre-wrap">Sentiment Radar | Score and subsequent returns — 23 September 2026

Felipe,

I added the relationship you requested between the current 0–100 attention &amp; sentiment score and the asset&#x27;s returns over the next 1 and 2 weeks. The email now includes a fixed-band reference table and each watchlist name&#x27;s own historical analogs. The radar also has two new return charts, historical dispersion, sample sizes and a 2024–25 versus 2026 comparison.

First finding: higher scores do not produce a consistently stronger return pattern in the retained USD universe. Across the full sample, the 80–100 band averaged +0.45% over 5 sessions and +1.97% over 10 sessions, versus all-band means of +0.89% and +1.91%. In 2026 alone, that high-score band averaged -0.33% and +1.46%, with both mean-confidence intervals spanning zero. This does not establish a robust positive leading-return signal.

The distinction between the pooled reference and each stock matters. At their current score bands, META has only one completed historical observation in this non-overlapping sample and LITE has none. Those cells are marked insufficient sample; the broader universe&#x27;s return is not substituted as a forecast for either name. The detailed study retains the observations for inspection.

The backtest uses the existing quantitative attention/tone score. Specialist-sales, SemiAnalysis and Damnang evidence remain in the qualitative review; there is no invented historical score for those comments. The study reuses cached data through 22 September and does not claim a new mailbox or market refresh.

Open the study:
http://DS-CAP-33:8080/wiki/_dashboards/attention-sentiment/score-returns.html
Main radar:
http://DS-CAP-33:8080/wiki/_dashboards/attention-sentiment/crowding-tracker.html

The next daily emails will include these tables automatically. This is a separate addition to today&#x27;s already delivered report.
</p><section id="score-return-email" style="background:var(--rd-soft);color:var(--rd-ink);padding:23px;font:14px/1.6 Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;border-radius:10px;margin-top:24px"><h2 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:21px;color:var(--rd-ink)">Score → next 1 and 2 weeks</h2><p>Prices through 2026-09-22. Historical conditional returns for the existing attention &amp; sentiment score (0–100), which blends attention and tone. Specialist-sales judgments are separate and are not retroactively scored. These means are reference analogs, not forecasts or price targets.</p><p>USD pooled reference: 75 historically eligible names. All-band means: 1w +0.9%; 2w +1.9%. N counts stock observations; shared market dates are not independent trials.</p><div class="rd-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Return data table" tabindex="0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;width:100%;font-family:Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif"><thead><tr><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">Score band</th><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">1w mean</th><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">1w median</th><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">1w up / N</th><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">2w mean</th><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">2w median</th><th style="background:#1b304b;color:#dce8f7;padding:9px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;text-align:left;font-size:12px">2w up / N</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">0–&lt;20</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+1.5%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.6%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">53% / 134</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+2.3%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.9%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">52% / 132</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">20–&lt;40</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+1.4%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.7%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">54% / 650</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+1.9%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+1.5%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">56% / 645</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">40–&lt;60</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.9%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.8%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">53% / 816</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+2.1%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+1.3%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">55% / 809</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">60–&lt;80</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.3%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">-0.0%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">50% / 622</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+1.5%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">-0.1%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">50% / 617</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">80–100</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.5%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+0.0%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">50% / 291</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">+2.0%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #3a4d66;color:var(--rd-ink);font-size:12px;white-spac